But it's not 12 points lost--the point made wasn't not to fooproof
things if you have tons of spare scrolls, it was that you shouldn't
bother until you've enchanted things.

Also, 12's high.  There are no gloves that are 2 AC, for instance.
It's unlikely that you'd want to waste scrolls on dwarvish helms or
iron shoe/high boots.  There's no body armor that I'd fooproof, either
(both mitril and DSM don't need it).  Really, the only things I'm
liable to want to fooproof eventually are 1 AC helm, 1 AC gloves, 1 AC
boots, 1 AC shield, and 1-2 AC cloak.  That's 5-6 points of AC--but
again, the point isn't that you shouldn't fooproof, it's that you
shouldn't fooproof until enchantment on your keeper items is maxed
out.

e.g. if you have a +3 pair of gloves and a spare ?ea, you could:
a) enchant them up.  They'll be at least AC5 (1 intrinsic, 4 magic)
now, and at least AC4 if you meet a rust monster or whatever; or
b) fooproof them. They'll be AC4 now and post-rust-monster.

In the former case, they're always at least as good and better in the
interim--and if you have a means of blessing the scroll, there's a
chance of even more AC.

Now, obviously, using c?destroy armor to fooproof is another story,
and once you've gotten things enchanted all the way up then
fooproofing becomes worthwile.



